%% generated by make_ol.py from src/T3.txt; edit the source, not this file

1. The legal doctrine under which a married woman's identity was absorbed into her husband's was called:
(A) Guardianship  (B) Primogeniture  (C) Suffrage  (D) Coverture
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Coverture^^ — Coverture.

2. The Seneca Falls Convention was held on:
(A) 4 July 1776  (B) 19–20 July 1848  (C) 8 March 1910  (D) 26 August 1920
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 19–20 July 1848^^ — 19–20 July 1848, New York.

3. The only African-American to sign the Declaration of Sentiments was:
(A) Sojourner Truth  (B) Booker T. Washington  (C) W. E. B. Du Bois  (D) Frederick Douglass
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Frederick Douglass^^ — Frederick Douglass.

4. The 19th Amendment, giving American women the vote, was ratified in:
(A) 1869  (B) 1893  (C) 1920  (D) 1928
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 1920^^ — 1920 (Wyoming Territory had given women the vote in 1869).

5. The first European country to give women both the vote and the right to stand was:
(A) Britain  (B) Sweden  (C) Norway  (D) Finland
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Finland^^ — Finland (1906).

6. The "Cat and Mouse Act" (1913) concerned:
(A) Hunger-striking suffragettes  (B) Women's property  (C) Child custody  (D) Divorce
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Hunger-striking suffragettes^^ — Released hunger strikers and re-arrested them.

7. Equal voting rights at 21 came to British women in:
(A) 1918  (B) 1920  (C) 1928  (D) 1945
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 1928^^ — 1928 (women over 30 with property voted from 1918).

8. The Egyptian Feminist Union (1923) was founded by:
(A) Huda Shaarawi  (B) Qasim Amin  (C) Nawal El Saadawi  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Huda Shaarawi^^ — Huda Shaarawi.

9. The 1968 strike that led to Britain's Equal Pay Act 1970 was by women at:
(A) Chiswick  (B) Rover Coventry  (C) Ruskin College  (D) Ford Dagenham
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Ford Dagenham^^ — Ford Dagenham machinists.

10. The first modern women's shelter opened in 1971 in:
(A) Toronto  (B) Stockholm  (C) New York  (D) Chiswick, London
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Chiswick, London^^ — Chiswick, London.

11. The opposition to the US Equal Rights Amendment was led by:
(A) Gloria Steinem  (B) Betty Friedan  (C) Phyllis Schlafly  (D) Bella Abzug
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Phyllis Schlafly^^ — Phyllis Schlafly; the ERA was never ratified.

12. Roe v. Wade was overturned in 2022 by:
(A) *Dobbs v. Jackson*  (B) *Planned Parenthood v. Casey*  (C) *Griswold v. Connecticut*  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) *Dobbs v. Jackson*^^ — *Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization* (2022).

13. *Backlash* (1991), describing the counter-attack on feminism in the 1980s, was written by:
(A) Naomi Wolf  (B) Angela McRobbie  (C) Rebecca Walker  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) None of these^^ — None of these — Susan Faludi.

14. The phrase "Me Too" was first used in 2006 by:
(A) Tarana Burke  (B) Alyssa Milano  (C) Laura Bates  (D) Anita Hill
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Tarana Burke^^ — Tarana Burke; #MeToo went global in October 2017.

15. SlutWalk began in 2011 in:
(A) London  (B) Toronto  (C) New Delhi  (D) Buenos Aires
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) Toronto^^ — Toronto.

16. #NiUnaMenos ("Not one less") began in 2015 in:
(A) Mexico  (B) Spain  (C) Argentina  (D) Chile
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Argentina^^ — Argentina.

17. The UN Commission on the Status of Women was set up in:
(A) 1945  (B) 1946  (C) 1975  (D) 1979
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 1946^^ — 1946.

18. The UN Decade for Women ran from:
(A) 1975–1985  (B) 1976–1985  (C) 1980–1990  (D) 1985–1995
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 1976–1985^^ — 1976–1985, after International Women's Year (1975).

19. Which is correct about CEDAW?
(A) It was adopted on 18 December 1979  (B) It entered into force on 3 September 1981  (C) Both A and B  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Both A and B^^ — Both: adopted 18 December 1979; in force 3 September 1981.

20. CEDAW's Article 14 concerns:
(A) Marriage and family  (B) Political life  (C) Temporary special measures  (D) Rural women
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Rural women^^ — Rural women (Art. 16 marriage; Art. 4 special measures; Art. 7 political life).

21. Pakistan's reservation to CEDAW concerns Article:
(A) 29(1)  (B) 16  (C) 4  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) 29(1)^^ — A reservation to Article 29(1), plus a general declaration.

22. CEDAW's Optional Protocol (1999), which Pakistan has not joined, allows:
(A) Individual complaints  (B) Reservations  (C) Country visits only  (D) Withdrawal
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Individual complaints^^ — Individual complaints.

23. The first head of UN Women (2010) was:
(A) Phumzile Mlambo-Ngcuka  (B) Michelle Bachelet  (C) Sima Bahous  (D) Emma Watson
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) Michelle Bachelet^^ — Michelle Bachelet.

24. The Muslim League formed its Central Women's Sub-Committee in 1938 at:
(A) Patna  (B) Lahore  (C) Aligarh  (D) Karachi
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Patna^^ — Patna.

25. The only Muslim woman delegate at the Round Table Conferences was:
(A) Fatima Jinnah  (B) Begum Ra'ana Liaquat Ali Khan  (C) Begum Jahanara Shahnawaz  (D) Begum Shaista Ikramullah
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Begum Jahanara Shahnawaz^^ — Begum Jahanara Shahnawaz.

26. Who hoisted the Muslim League flag on the Punjab Civil Secretariat in 1947?
(A) Fatima Jinnah  (B) Fatima Sughra  (C) Salma Tasadduq Hussain  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) Fatima Sughra^^ — Fatima Sughra.

27. PM Bogra's second marriage (1955) led to the commission on marriage and family laws headed by:
(A) Justice Rashid  (B) Justice Munir  (C) Justice Cornelius  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Justice Rashid^^ — The Rashid Commission, which led to the MFLO 1961.

28. The Women's Action Forum was founded in Karachi in 1981 after the case of:
(A) Safia Bibi  (B) Fehmida and Allah Bux  (C) Saima Waheed  (D) Mukhtaran Mai
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) Fehmida and Allah Bux^^ — The Fehmida–Allah Bux case.

29. 12 February became Pakistan's National Women's Day in:
(A) 1983  (B) 2002  (C) 2012  (D) 2018
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 2012^^ — 2012, commemorating the Lahore protest of 12 February 1983.

30. The mass movement of rural Sindhi women from 1982 was the:
(A) Lady Health Workers' movement  (B) Aurat March  (C) Sindhiani Tehreek  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Sindhiani Tehreek^^ — Sindhiani Tehreek.

31. Al-Huda was founded in 1994 by:
(A) Riffat Hassan  (B) Asma Jahangir  (C) Hina Jilani  (D) Farhat Hashmi
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Farhat Hashmi^^ — Farhat Hashmi.

32. Writers on the "NGO-isation" of women's movements include:
(A) Moser and Molyneux  (B) Sonia Alvarez and Islah Jad  (C) Bowles and Klein  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) Sonia Alvarez and Islah Jad^^ — Sonia Alvarez (1999) and Islah Jad (2004).
